WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.077 --> 00:00:05.281
After work Ally rushed home to tell Mateo her worries about Tina.

2
00:00:05.282 --> 00:00:10.819
"Maybe it's another misunderstanding, like with Melanie," Mateo said.

3
00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:14.906
"Maybe." Ally started pacing.

4
00:00:14.907 --> 00:00:19.458
"I can't think straight knowing there's a Jorgandian in Sandville!"

5
00:00:19.459 --> 00:00:24.918
"Alpha, have you found any more clues about the Jorgandian?" Mateo asked.

6
00:00:24.919 --> 00:00:33.864
"I have scanned approximately 234 life-forms," Alpha said. She printed out a list.

7
00:00:33.865 --> 00:00:43.034
Ally recognized lots of names, including the mayor, employees at Pepe's, and many of Ray's regular customers.

8
00:00:43.035 --> 00:00:49.799
"But, Alpha, there are a lot more than 234 people in Sandville," Mateo said.

9
00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:52.989
"Have you scanned Tina?" Ally asked.

10
00:00:52.990 --> 00:00:57.973
"She's that new security guard at the museum, and she seems suspicious."

11
00:00:57.974 --> 00:01:03.159
"Negative. The museum is too far for my limited scanning ability."

12
00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:08.361
"Please try harder," Ally said. "This is important!"

13
00:01:08.362 --> 00:01:14.048
Alpha looked annoyed. "Have you tried to read this life-form's mind?"

14
00:01:14.049 --> 00:01:22.125
"Uh . . . no," Ally said. "I didn't think of her as a suspect until after she left the diner."

15
00:01:22.126 --> 00:01:27.188
"Hmpf!" Alpha snorted. "Try harder, Allyzooba!"

16
00:01:27.189 --> 00:01:30.814
"I'm not a computer," Ally snapped. "And—"

17
00:01:30.815 --> 00:01:35.222
"We're all on the same team," Mateo interrupted.

18
00:01:35.223 --> 00:01:40.446
"Alpha, how accurate would your scans be if someone was in close range?"

19
00:01:40.447 --> 00:01:43.956
"One hundred percent accuracy."

20
00:01:43.957 --> 00:01:48.919
"It's too bad Alpha's not in a phone anymore," Mateo said.

21
00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:54.039
"Then you could bring her into town with you, Ally, and she could scan lots of people."

22
00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:59.307
"That is too bad . . ." Ally got an idea.

23
00:01:59.308 --> 00:02:05.102
"I can still do that! Did Ray buy a new computer yet?"

24
00:02:05.103 --> 00:02:07.376
"Nope," Mateo said.

25
00:02:07.377 --> 00:02:13.724
"Then let's use Alpha! I'll tell him he can borrow mine until he buys one.

26
00:02:13.725 --> 00:02:17.188
That way Alpha can scan more people."

27
00:02:17.189 --> 00:02:22.817
"Are you sure?" Mateo asked. "She still glitches sometimes."

28
00:02:22.818 --> 00:02:28.588
Alpha's screen flashed. "That is because I'm trapped in this primitive Earthling machine.

29
00:02:28.589 --> 00:02:31.723
But, Allyzooba, you have a valid idea.

30
00:02:31.724 --> 00:02:36.559
If you bring me to Ray's, I will be able to scan all customers in the diner.

31
00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:41.847
I can also scan all life-forms in the general vicinity."

32
00:02:41.848 --> 00:02:44.759
Ally beamed, and so did Mateo.

33
00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:50.007
"Great!" he said. "I'll tell Papi to hold off on buying a new computer.

34
00:02:50.008 --> 00:02:56.653
We can bring Alpha to the diner tomorrow."

35
00:02:56.654 --> 00:03:03.877
*** The next morning Ally and Mateo set up Alpha in Ray's

36
00:03:03.878 --> 00:03:06.821
office. "Thanks for lending me your computer," Ray said.

37
00:03:06.822 --> 00:03:09.999
"It will be a good test to see if I need to buy a new one."

38
00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:13.799
"We can show you how it works, Papi," Mateo said.

39
00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:15.851
"Maybe later," Ray said.

40
00:03:15.852 --> 00:03:19.259
"I need to get ready for my meeting with the CEO of Big City Foods.

41
00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:22.189
I want to make him a special meal."

42
00:03:22.190 --> 00:03:26.879
Ally waited for Ray to go into the kitchen, then she spoke to Alpha.

43
00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:32.217
"Now remember, Alpha. If you find a Jorgandian, chime once.

44
00:03:32.218 --> 00:03:36.971
But no talking while you're here. None. Understood?"

45
00:03:36.972 --> 00:03:39.080
Alpha didn't reply.

46
00:03:39.081 --> 00:03:42.327
"Alpha, did you hear me?" Ally repeated.

47
00:03:42.328 --> 00:03:44.981
Again Alpha did not respond.

48
00:03:44.982 --> 00:03:51.385
Ally rolled her eyes. "You can speak now, so I know you're working."

49
00:03:51.386 --> 00:03:56.768
"Of course, I'm working!" Alpha said just as Flo came into the office.

50
00:03:56.769 --> 00:04:02.323
"Wow!" Flo laughed when she saw the computer.

51
00:04:02.324 --> 00:04:06.559
"I can't believe Ray is joining the twenty-first century.

52
00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:10.110
I thought he'd never get a new computer!"

53
00:04:10.111 --> 00:04:16.046
"He's thinking about buying a new one, so Ally loaned hers to him," Mateo said.

54
00:04:16.047 --> 00:04:21.718
"Hello!" Phil called from the dining room. "Anybody here?"

55
00:04:21.719 --> 00:04:25.468
They all hurried back into the dining room.

56
00:04:25.469 --> 00:04:31.822
"Hi, Phil," Ally said nervously. "Uh . . . where's Tina?"

57
00:04:31.823 --> 00:04:35.339
"She's meeting with Dr. Lloyd in his lab," Phil said.

58
00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:38.112
"He's telling her about his research."

59
00:04:38.113 --> 00:04:46.357
"Oh right," Ally said. "She mentioned that. Do you think she'll be in later?"

60
00:04:46.358 --> 00:04:48.985
Phil shrugged. "Maybe."

61
00:04:48.986 --> 00:04:53.382
Ally and Mateo exchanged uneasy looks.

62
00:04:53.383 --> 00:04:59.379
They needed Tina to come into the diner today so Alpha could scan her.

63
00:04:59.380 --> 00:05:06.404
Suddenly Mateo grinned. "Oh, Phil! You should tell Tina about our new policy at Ray's.

64
00:05:06.405 --> 00:05:10.677
We offer a free lunch to new residents of Sandville."

65
00:05:10.678 --> 00:05:14.719
"Ooh!" Phil said. "I'll send her in at lunchtime.

66
00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:18.519
Now can I give you my breakfast order?"

67
00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:25.439
While Flo took his order, Mateo gestured to Ally.

68
00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:32.279
"I'll come back at lunchtime," he whispered. "In case you—" Ping!

69
00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:34.375
Mateo looked at his phone.

70
00:05:34.376 --> 00:05:40.438
"It's a text from Coach. He needs me to take over a camp session for the little kids.

71
00:05:40.439 --> 00:05:43.169
There's something going on with his brother.

72
00:05:43.170 --> 00:05:46.440
They never argue, but they just had a big fight.

73
00:05:46.441 --> 00:05:50.291
Coach is going to the copy shop to smooth things over."

74
00:05:50.292 --> 00:06:01.820
"No problem." Ally said. "As long as Alpha behaves herself!"

